window.QUIZ2_BANK.push(...[{"id":801,"targetId":801,"type":"tc","text":"Her plan to provide every household with free electricity was generous but {{1}}: the proposed power station could not supply even one village.","choices":[["quixotic","parsimonious","practicable","mercenary","retrospective"]],"answers":[["quixotic"]],"explanation":"The contrast is between admirable intentions and impossible implementation. Quixotic captures that impractical idealism; the other choices concern thrift, practicality, profit, or the past.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"q"},{"id":802,"targetId":802,"type":"tc","text":"The reform was {{1}}, not cosmetic: it abolished the inherited hierarchy rather than merely renaming its offices.","choices":[["radical","nominal","incremental","peripheral","temporary"]],"answers":[["radical"]],"explanation":"Abolishing the system changes its foundations. Radical fits this fundamental transformation; the alternatives describe limited, marginal, or short-lived changes.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":803,"targetId":803,"type":"tc","text":"The closure saved the firm money, but an unforeseen {{1}} was the disappearance of the town’s only apprenticeship program.","choices":[["ramification","premise","precedent","stipulation","analogy"]],"answers":[["ramification"]],"explanation":"The disappearance followed from the closure, making it a consequence or ramification, not an initial assumption, condition, or comparison.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":804,"targetId":804,"type":"tc","text":"Even after acquiring more land than he could cultivate, the {{1}} proprietor continued to seize his neighbors’ fields.","choices":[["rapacious","abstemious","indifferent","magnanimous","impecunious"]],"answers":[["rapacious"]],"explanation":"Continued seizure despite having ample land indicates aggressive greed. The other traits do not explain this appetite for acquisition.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":805,"targetId":805,"type":"tc","text":"Although her conclusion offended popular sentiment, the committee conceded that it was {{1}}, following step by step from independently verified premises.","choices":[["rational","arbitrary","intuitive","capricious","fallacious"]],"answers":[["rational"]],"explanation":"Logical derivation from verified premises supports rational. Popular approval is irrelevant; arbitrary, intuitive, capricious, and fallacious do not describe this reasoning.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":806,"targetId":806,"type":"tc","text":"Conservationists removed the invasive beetle before it could {{1}} the orchard, where its larvae were capable of killing every mature tree.","choices":[["ravage","propagate","irrigate","replenish","adorn"]],"answers":[["ravage"]],"explanation":"The threat is severe destruction, so ravage fits. The other verbs involve growing, watering, restocking, or decorating rather than destroying trees.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":807,"targetId":807,"type":"tc","text":"Presented with the original ledger, the witness agreed to {{1}} his earlier accusation, explicitly stating that it had been false.","choices":[["recant","substantiate","reiterate","embellish","qualify"]],"answers":[["recant"]],"explanation":"An explicit withdrawal of a false statement is recanting. Qualifying would only limit it, while the other choices retain or reinforce it.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":808,"targetId":808,"type":"tc","text":"The historian’s task was to {{1}} two apparently incompatible accounts by showing that their authors had described different stages of the same battle.","choices":[["reconcile","discredit","juxtapose","suppress","truncate"]],"answers":[["reconcile"]],"explanation":"Showing how both accounts can be true makes them consistent. Merely juxtaposing them would not resolve their apparent incompatibility.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":809,"targetId":809,"type":"tc","text":"The footnotes concerned such {{1}} disputes in medieval theology that even specialists in the period needed a glossary.","choices":[["recondite","hackneyed","transparent","elementary","contemporary"]],"answers":[["recondite"]],"explanation":"Even specialists’ need for explanation signals obscure, difficult material. The other choices imply familiarity, clarity, simplicity, or modernity.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":810,"targetId":810,"type":"tc","text":"Once the internal appeal had failed, the dismissed employee’s only remaining {{1}} was an independent tribunal.","choices":[["recourse","liability","pretext","impediment","recompense"]],"answers":[["recourse"]],"explanation":"The tribunal is an avenue for seeking a remedy, not itself compensation, a debt, an excuse, or an obstacle.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":811,"targetId":811,"type":"tc","text":"After a decade in which no cases were reported, the {{1}} disease prompted the reopening of surveillance stations.","choices":[["recrudescent","eradicated","congenital","benign","spurious"]],"answers":[["recrudescent"]],"explanation":"The disease has broken out again after apparent relief. Recrudescent expresses recurrence; the other choices describe elimination, origin at birth, harmlessness, or falsity.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":812,"targetId":812,"type":"tc","text":"Her opponents mocked her small staff, but none underestimated the {{1}} advocate whose previous arguments had overturned three major laws.","choices":[["redoubtable","ineffectual","diffident","inconsequential","compliant"]],"answers":[["redoubtable"]],"explanation":"Her record makes her formidable and deserving of respect. Small staff size does not make her weak, timid, unimportant, or obedient.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":813,"targetId":813,"type":"tc","text":"The second experiment was intended to {{1}} the estimate: the phenomenon was already established, but its magnitude remained imprecisely known.","choices":[["refine","invalidate","conceal","inflate","abandon"]],"answers":[["refine"]],"explanation":"The goal is greater precision, not rejection or artificial enlargement. Refine fits improving an existing estimate.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":814,"targetId":814,"type":"tc","text":"A single verified counterexample suffices to {{1}} the claim that every specimen has exactly six legs.","choices":[["refute","corroborate","illustrate","restate","extrapolate"]],"answers":[["refute"]],"explanation":"A universal claim is false if one genuine exception exists. Refute expresses that logical defeat; the alternatives do not.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":815,"targetId":815,"type":"tc","text":"Without continued practice, the patient might {{1}} to the limited mobility observed before treatment rather than retain her recent gains.","choices":[["regress","ascend","adapt","proceed","diversify"]],"answers":[["regress"]],"explanation":"Returning to a previous, worse state is regression. The contrast with retaining gains rules out progress or simple adaptation.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":816,"targetId":816,"type":"tc","text":"Because several reporters had missed the qualification, the scientist paused to {{1}} that the finding applied only to adults.","choices":[["reiterate","retract","disavow","obscure","contest"]],"answers":[["reiterate"]],"explanation":"The qualification must be said again, not withdrawn, denied, hidden, or challenged. Reiterate means repeat for emphasis.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":817,"targetId":817,"type":"tc","text":"Editors refused to {{1}} the discovery to a brief footnote; they believed it warranted the opening chapter.","choices":[["relegate","elevate","attribute","restore","translate"]],"answers":[["relegate"]],"explanation":"A footnote is a lesser position than an opening chapter. Relegate means assign to that lower status; elevate reverses the direction.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":818,"targetId":818,"type":"tc","text":"The landlord initially rejected every request for an extension, but finally agreed to {{1}} when shown proof of the bank’s error.","choices":[["relent","persist","retaliate","prevaricate","intervene"]],"answers":[["relent"]],"explanation":"Agreement after repeated refusal signals yielding or becoming less severe. Persist would retain the refusal; the other actions do not express this reversal.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":819,"targetId":819,"type":"tc","text":"Unlike her predecessor, who retained informal authority after retirement, the director chose to {{1}} all control over appointments.","choices":[["relinquish","consolidate","exercise","legitimize","augment"]],"answers":[["relinquish"]],"explanation":"The contrast requires giving control up entirely. The other verbs involve keeping, using, justifying, or increasing power.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":820,"targetId":820,"type":"tc","text":"Far from resenting the difficult objections, the philosopher seemed to {{1}} them, calling vigorous criticism the most enjoyable part of her work.","choices":[["relish","forestall","deplore","evade","tolerate"]],"answers":[["relish"]],"explanation":"Calling criticism enjoyable implies active pleasure, stronger than merely tolerating it. The other choices express avoidance or disapproval.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":821,"targetId":821,"type":"tc","text":"The course was {{1}}, designed to repair gaps in basic arithmetic; its instructor used an {{2}} tone so that returning students would not feel humiliated.","choices":[["remedial","celebratory","speculative"],["anodyne","acrimonious","imperious"]],"answers":[["remedial"],["anodyne"]],"explanation":"Repairing deficiencies makes the course remedial. Avoiding humiliation calls for an inoffensive, soothing tone rather than bitterness or domination.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"anodyne","meaning":"Soothing or unlikely to cause offense"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":822,"targetId":822,"type":"tc","text":"The trustees increased the researcher’s {{1}}, but their accompanying letter was anything but {{2}}: it itemized serious doubts about her methods.","choices":[["remuneration","jurisdiction","probation"],["approbatory","censorious","skeptical"]],"answers":[["remuneration"],["approbatory"]],"explanation":"The first blank concerns payment. “Anything but” requires a quality contradicted by the criticism: the letter was not approving, though censorious and skeptical would describe it directly.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"approbatory","meaning":"Expressing favorable judgment"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":823,"targetId":823,"type":"tc","text":"Leaving the instrument in salt water would {{1}} it useless; consequently, the warning label’s apparently {{2}} language was justified by a real risk of total failure.","choices":[["render","reconcile","replenish"],["baleful","jubilant","euphemistic"]],"answers":[["render"],["baleful"]],"explanation":"Render means cause to become. A warning of complete failure is threatening or baleful; delight and softened wording do not fit the stated severity.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"baleful","meaning":"Menacing or suggestive of harm"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":824,"targetId":824,"type":"tc","text":"The contractor threatened to {{1}} on the agreement unless the city accepted a surcharge that auditors considered {{2}}, since it exceeded the entire original budget.","choices":[["renege","deliberate","embark"],["unconscionable","negligible","commensurate"]],"answers":[["renege"],["unconscionable"]],"explanation":"Backing out of an agreement is reneging. A surcharge larger than the whole budget is presented as outrageously excessive, not tiny or proportionate.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"unconscionable","meaning":"So unfair or excessive as to offend conscience"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":825,"targetId":825,"type":"tc","text":"When she chose to {{1}} the movement’s doctrines, her former allies branded her an {{2}}, even though she still admired its early achievements.","choices":[["renounce","disseminate","codify"],["apostate","acolyte","arbiter"]],"answers":[["renounce"],["apostate"]],"explanation":"Formally rejecting doctrines is renouncing them; someone who abandons a cause is an apostate. Continued admiration for past achievements does not negate that departure.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"apostate","meaning":"Someone who abandons a faith or cause"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":826,"targetId":826,"type":"tc","text":"The most damaging {{1}} of the insult was a boycott; its organizer was openly {{2}}, declaring that the sole purpose was to make the offending company suffer.","choices":[["repercussion","antecedent","exemption"],["vindictive","conciliatory","disinterested"]],"answers":[["repercussion"],["vindictive"]],"explanation":"The boycott is a harmful consequence, not a preceding event or exemption. An avowed wish to punish identifies vindictiveness, not reconciliation or impartiality.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"vindictive","meaning":"Intent on retaliating for an injury"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":827,"targetId":827,"type":"tc","text":"The actor’s expanding {{1}} reflected his desire to {{2}} with established performers for leading roles: he mastered tragedy as well as comedy.","choices":[["repertoire","remuneration","seclusion"],["vie","commiserate","comply"]],"answers":[["repertoire"],["vie"]],"explanation":"A range of mastered performance types is a repertoire. Seeking the same leading roles as established actors means competing, or vying, rather than sympathizing or obeying.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"vie","meaning":"Compete with others for something"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":828,"targetId":828,"type":"tc","text":"Although donors agreed to {{1}} the emergency fund, none would {{2}} its continuing expenses; a one-time gift was all they promised.","choices":[["replenish","deplete","audit"],["underwrite","curtail","itemize"]],"answers":[["replenish"],["underwrite"]],"explanation":"The gifts restore the depleted fund. The contrast limits that support: donors refuse ongoing financial backing, which is underwriting, not cutting or listing expenses.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"underwrite","meaning":"Provide financial backing for"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":829,"targetId":829,"type":"tc","text":"The mentor meant to {{1}} the apprentice for concealing the error, yet avoided {{2}} because a harsh manner would make future honesty less likely.","choices":[["reproach","commend","exonerate"],["asperity","leniency","candor"]],"answers":[["reproach"],["asperity"]],"explanation":"Concealing the error merits disapproval. The mentor deliberately avoids harshness while remaining honest, so asperity, not candor, names the excluded manner.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"asperity","meaning":"Harshness in speech or manner"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":830,"targetId":830,"type":"tc","text":"The scientist was quick to {{1}} the forged endorsement, recognizing it as an {{2}} designed to lend credibility to an otherwise unsupported product.","choices":[["repudiate","authenticate","circulate"],["artifice","apothegm","atavism"]],"answers":[["repudiate"],["artifice"]],"explanation":"She rejects a false endorsement rather than certifying or spreading it. A deliberate credibility trick is artifice, not a maxim or ancestral recurrence.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"artifice","meaning":"A device or trick used to mislead"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":831,"targetId":831,"type":"tc","text":"The torture was {{1}} to the investigator, but she resisted an {{2}} account that merely called its perpetrators monsters; she wanted an explanation of how the system had enabled them.","choices":[["repugnant","salutary","endearing"],["vacuous","analytical","illuminating"]],"answers":[["repugnant"],["vacuous"]],"explanation":"Torture provokes disgust. “Merely” labeling people provides no explanation, so the account is empty of analysis; illuminating or analytical would contradict the deficiency.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"vacuous","meaning":"Empty of meaningful ideas"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":832,"targetId":832,"type":"tc","text":"The institution proved {{1}}, reopening within weeks of the disaster, but its recovery was not a mere {{2}}: independent audits confirmed that its core services were functioning.","choices":[["resilient","moribund","inert"],["veneer","foundation","impediment"]],"answers":[["resilient"],["veneer"]],"explanation":"Rapid recovery demonstrates resilience. The audits show that recovery is real rather than a deceptive outward appearance, which a veneer would be.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"veneer","meaning":"An outward covering that conceals the underlying reality"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":833,"targetId":833,"type":"tc","text":"The minister remained {{1}} in opposing the ban; her colleagues described her position as {{2}}, since no proposed concession could move her.","choices":[["resolute","ambivalent","compliant"],["uncompromising","equivocal","provisional"]],"answers":[["resolute"],["uncompromising"]],"explanation":"Firm opposition and refusal of every concession support both resolute and uncompromising. Hesitation, ambiguity, obedience, and provisionality conflict with the evidence.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"uncompromising","meaning":"Unwilling to make concessions"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":834,"targetId":834,"type":"tc","text":"The audience grew {{1}} during the unexplained delay, and soon became so {{2}} that the ushers could no longer keep people in their seats.","choices":[["restive","somnolent","contented"],["unruly","tractable","deferential"]],"answers":[["restive"],["unruly"]],"explanation":"Impatience develops into resistance to control. Restive and unruly fit this progression; sleepiness, contentment, and obedience do not.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"unruly","meaning":"Resisting discipline or control"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":835,"targetId":835,"type":"tc","text":"Normally {{1}} about her private life, the author found the interviewer’s persistent questions likely to {{2}} her rather than draw out a relaxed conversation.","choices":[["reticent","garrulous","forthcoming"],["unnerve","reassure","placate"]],"answers":[["reticent"],["unnerve"]],"explanation":"A reluctance to disclose personal matters identifies reticence. Persistent intrusion would unsettle her, not calm or reassure her.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"unnerve","meaning":"Shake someone’s confidence or composure"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":836,"targetId":836,"type":"tc","text":"The {{1}} scholar avoided receptions, yet his {{2}} appetite for archives made him indefatigable at research; only through books did he enjoy the {{3}} adventures of explorers.","choices":[["retiring","gregarious","ostentatious"],["voracious","tepid","stinting"],["vicarious","firsthand","autobiographical"]],"answers":[["retiring"],["voracious"],["vicarious"]],"explanation":"His avoidance of social events makes him retiring. Indefatigable reading reflects a voracious appetite. Adventures experienced through books rather than participation are vicarious.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"voracious","meaning":"Consuming or seeking something with great eagerness"},{"word":"vicarious","meaning":"Experienced through another person rather than directly"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":837,"targetId":837,"type":"tc","text":"The mayor’s {{1}} promised equality, but his {{2}} administration excluded all dissent; the gap between language and practice made the promised reform seem {{3}}.","choices":[["rhetoric","reticence","recompense"],["autocratic","collegial","decentralized"],["illusory","inevitable","consummate"]],"answers":[["rhetoric"],["autocratic"],["illusory"]],"explanation":"Rhetoric is the public persuasive language. Excluding every dissenting voice is autocratic. That contradiction makes the announced equality an illusion, not an inevitable or completed achievement.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"autocratic","meaning":"Exercising power without allowing others a say"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":838,"targetId":838,"type":"tc","text":"The study’s {{1}} impressed reviewers: identical procedures kept measurement {{2}} low, while transparent records prevented even a suspicion of {{3}}.","choices":[["rigor","levity","obscurity"],["variance","credence","fervor"],["artifice","candor","diligence"]],"answers":[["rigor"],["variance"],["artifice"]],"explanation":"Precision and strict procedure constitute rigor. Consistent measurement reduces variation. Transparency prevents suspicion of deceptive contrivance, not honesty or careful work.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"variance","meaning":"Difference or variation"},{"word":"artifice","meaning":"A device or trick used to mislead"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":839,"targetId":839,"type":"tc","text":"The software was {{1}} enough to survive repeated attacks, but the vendor’s claim that it was wholly invulnerable was {{2}} exaggeration; such boasts could only {{3}} complacency.","choices":[["robust","brittle","nascent"],["arrant","tentative","measured"],["engender","dispel","preclude"]],"answers":[["robust"],["arrant"],["engender"]],"explanation":"Survival under attack shows robustness. Complete invulnerability is an outright, arrant exaggeration. Overconfidence produces complacency rather than dispelling or preventing it.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"arrant","meaning":"Utter; complete, usually in a negative description"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":840,"targetId":840,"type":"tc","text":"The apprentice’s {{1}} technique was still crude, but her confidence began to {{2}} after small successes; her teacher therefore refused to {{3}} her early mistakes as evidence of permanent incapacity.","choices":[["rudimentary","consummate","sophisticated"],["wax","wane","stagnate"],["construe","expunge","condone"]],"answers":[["rudimentary"],["wax"],["construe"]],"explanation":"Crude early technique is rudimentary. Success increases confidence, so wax is required. The teacher refuses to interpret, or construe, errors as permanent incapacity; erasing or excusing errors is a different action.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"wax","meaning":"Grow in strength or intensity"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":841,"targetId":841,"type":"se","text":"Rather than issue a hurried reply, the judge chose to {{1}} on the implications of the testimony before announcing a decision.","choices":[["ruminate","meditate","improvise","expatiate","equivocate","harangue"]],"answers":[["ruminate","meditate"]],"explanation":"Ruminate and meditate both mean reflect deeply here. The sentence requires private consideration, not spontaneous action, extended speech, evasion, or a tirade.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"meditate","meaning":"Reflect deeply"}],"section":17,"initial":"r"},{"id":842,"targetId":842,"type":"se","text":"The warden’s {{1}} behavior went beyond enforcing rules: he deliberately prolonged punishments because the prisoners’ anguish delighted him.","choices":[["sadistic","cruel","scrupulous","diffident","indulgent","equitable"]],"answers":[["sadistic","cruel"]],"explanation":"Sadistic and cruel both describe the deliberate infliction of suffering in this context. Pleasure in anguish excludes fairness, indulgence, and conscientious rule enforcement.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"cruel","meaning":"Deliberately causing suffering"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":843,"targetId":843,"type":"se","text":"By identifying the flaw that every other adviser had missed and proposing a workable correction, the apparently inexperienced consultant proved unexpectedly {{1}}.","choices":[["sagacious","perspicacious","credulous","impetuous","inflexible","garrulous"]],"answers":[["sagacious","perspicacious"]],"explanation":"Sagacious and perspicacious both describe perceptive good judgment. Discovering a hidden flaw and correcting it supplies evidence of discernment, not gullibility or mere talkativeness.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"perspicacious","meaning":"Quick to perceive and judge accurately"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":844,"targetId":844,"type":"se","text":"Compared with the smoke-filled dormitory, the new residence offered a distinctly {{1}} environment, with clean air and abundant natural light.","choices":[["salubrious","healthful","opulent","secluded","austere","precarious"]],"answers":[["salubrious","healthful"]],"explanation":"Salubrious and healthful identify the improved conditions for health. Clean air and light do not establish luxury, isolation, austerity, or insecurity.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"healthful","meaning":"Conducive to good health"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":845,"targetId":845,"type":"se","text":"Though embarrassing at the time, the failed rehearsal had a {{1}} effect, exposing faults the orchestra could correct before the premiere.","choices":[["salutary","beneficial","deleterious","transient","pernicious","incidental"]],"answers":[["salutary","beneficial"]],"explanation":"Salutary and beneficial both capture the useful corrective effect. The embarrassment does not negate the practical improvement, and the sentence gives no basis for a merely fleeting or incidental effect.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"beneficial","meaning":"Producing a helpful effect"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":846,"targetId":846,"type":"se","text":"His {{1}} lectures about honesty irritated colleagues who knew that he routinely manipulated the accounts for his own benefit.","choices":[["sanctimonious","self-righteous","contrite","diffident","irreverent","circumspect"]],"answers":[["sanctimonious","self-righteous"]],"explanation":"Sanctimonious and self-righteous both convey the assumed moral superiority undermined by his behavior. Repentance or caution would not explain these hypocritical lectures.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"self-righteous","meaning":"Convinced of one’s own moral superiority"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":847,"targetId":847,"type":"se","text":"The board refused to {{1}} the experiment until the researchers had obtained written consent from every participant.","choices":[["sanction","authorize","penalize","replicate","censure","publicize"]],"answers":[["sanction","authorize"]],"explanation":"Sanction and authorize mean grant permission in this context. Consent is a prerequisite to approval, not to criticism, punishment, replication, or publicity.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"authorize","meaning":"Give official permission"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":848,"targetId":848,"type":"se","text":"Even after two disappointing trials, the engineer remained {{1}} about the design, confidently predicting success after one minor adjustment.","choices":[["sanguine","optimistic","resigned","apprehensive","indifferent","distrustful"]],"answers":[["sanguine","optimistic"]],"explanation":"Sanguine and optimistic both express favorable expectations. Confidently predicting success directly rules out resignation, anxiety, indifference, and distrust.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"optimistic","meaning":"Expecting a favorable outcome"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":849,"targetId":849,"type":"se","text":"By depicting officials who solemnly debate the proper color of a sinking ship, the cartoon adopts a {{1}} attitude toward bureaucratic priorities.","choices":[["satirical","mocking","reverential","documentary","nostalgic","conciliatory"]],"answers":[["satirical","mocking"]],"explanation":"Satirical and mocking both express ridicule of misplaced priorities. The absurd scene exposes folly rather than honoring, neutrally recording, or reconciling officials.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"mocking","meaning":"Ridiculing something"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":850,"targetId":850,"type":"se","text":"The surviving evidence is so {{1}} that any detailed reconstruction of the ceremony would owe more to imagination than to the archive.","choices":[["scant","meager","equivocal","voluminous","fabricated","systematic"]],"answers":[["scant","meager"]],"explanation":"Scant and meager both mean insufficient in quantity. The need to invent detail follows from a shortage of evidence, not necessarily ambiguity, fabrication, or organization.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"meager","meaning":"Insufficient in amount"}],"section":17,"initial":"s"},{"id":851,"targetId":851,"type":"tc","text":"The critic’s assessment was {{1}}: she called the book intellectually dishonest and dismissed its central argument as an elaborate fraud.","choices":[["scathing","laudatory","equivocal","restrained","perfunctory"]],"answers":[["scathing"]],"explanation":"The emphatic denunciation is severely critical. Scathing fits; praise, uncertainty, restraint, and superficial attention do not capture its force.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":852,"targetId":852,"type":"tc","text":"Disagreement over doctrine produced a permanent {{1}}, with each faction establishing its own institutions and refusing communion with the other.","choices":[["schism","consensus","truce","hierarchy","repertoire"]],"answers":[["schism"]],"explanation":"A lasting division into separate factions is a schism. Consensus and truce imply agreement or peace, while hierarchy and repertoire describe different structures.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":853,"targetId":853,"type":"tc","text":"The conversation became {{1}} when the usually silent novelist joined in, answering each observation with an original and dazzlingly witty rejoinder.","choices":[["scintillating","desultory","soporific","acrimonious","pedestrian"]],"answers":[["scintillating"]],"explanation":"Dazzling wit makes conversation scintillating. The sentence describes neither aimlessness, sleepiness, hostility, nor dull ordinariness.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":854,"targetId":854,"type":"tc","text":"Her dismissal of the proposal as beneath serious consideration revealed {{1}}, not merely disagreement about its cost.","choices":[["scorn","ambivalence","solicitude","deference","astonishment"]],"answers":[["scorn"]],"explanation":"Treating a proposal as beneath consideration expresses contempt. A cost disagreement alone would not imply this disrespect.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":855,"targetId":855,"type":"tc","text":"Because the archivist was {{1}} about ownership, she returned even the smallest unrecorded donation until its provenance had been established.","choices":[["scrupulous","cavalier","expedient","credulous","erratic"]],"answers":[["scrupulous"]],"explanation":"Refusing to overlook ownership questions demonstrates conscientious care. Carelessness, convenience, gullibility, and inconsistency conflict with her systematic conduct.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":856,"targetId":856,"type":"tc","text":"The editor’s {{1}} comparison of every quotation with the original manuscript took months, but it eliminated dozens of inherited errors.","choices":[["sedulous","desultory","cursory","intermittent","improvised"]],"answers":[["sedulous"]],"explanation":"Checking every quotation over months requires persistent diligence. The alternatives imply casualness, brevity, irregularity, or lack of preparation.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":857,"targetId":857,"type":"tc","text":"The newspaper ignored the report’s sober conclusion and selected its most {{1}} details, hoping lurid disclosures would increase sales.","choices":[["sensational","prosaic","technical","inconspicuous","reassuring"]],"answers":[["sensational"]],"explanation":"Lurid disclosures are intended to arouse intense interest. Technicality or reassurance is not the identified source of appeal.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":858,"targetId":858,"type":"tc","text":"The memoir’s ending struck even sympathetic readers as excessively {{1}}: every reconciliation elicited tears, and no troublesome feeling survived the final embrace.","choices":[["sentimental","analytical","dispassionate","caustic","elliptical"]],"answers":[["sentimental"]],"explanation":"Excessive emotion and effortless reconciliation indicate sentimentality. Analysis, detachment, bitterness, and omission do not describe the treatment.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":859,"targetId":859,"type":"tc","text":"Despite the surrounding commotion, the negotiator remained {{1}}, speaking in an even voice and showing no trace of agitation.","choices":[["serene","restive","ebullient","choleric","distracted"]],"answers":[["serene"]],"explanation":"Calm speech and absence of agitation support serene. Restlessness, excitement, anger, and distraction conflict with that composure.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":860,"targetId":860,"type":"tc","text":"The trustees voted to {{1}} all ties with the fraudulent charity, ending both funding and joint projects immediately.","choices":[["sever","strengthen","conceal","formalize","mediate"]],"answers":[["sever"]],"explanation":"Ending every connection means severing ties. Strengthening and formalizing do the opposite; concealment would preserve them secretly.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":861,"targetId":861,"type":"tc","text":"The advertised competition was a {{1}}: the winner had been selected before any applications were received.","choices":[["sham","stalemate","windfall","precedent","deterrent"]],"answers":[["sham"]],"explanation":"A preselected winner makes the competition a fraudulent pretense. The other nouns do not express false appearance.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":862,"targetId":862,"type":"tc","text":"As evidence for his position weakened, the commentator’s tone grew increasingly {{1}}, replacing reasoned explanation with piercing accusations shouted over his guests.","choices":[["shrill","measured","mellifluous","reticent","conciliatory"]],"answers":[["shrill"]],"explanation":"Piercing, shouted accusations indicate a strident tone. The alternatives suggest moderation, pleasant sound, silence, or reconciliation.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":863,"targetId":863,"type":"tc","text":"Asked directly who authorized the payment, the spokesperson tried to {{1}} the issue by discussing the agency’s unrelated achievements.","choices":[["skirt","resolve","clarify","foreground","adjudicate"]],"answers":[["skirt"]],"explanation":"Changing to unrelated achievements avoids the question. The other verbs would engage with or settle the issue.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":864,"targetId":864,"type":"tc","text":"Investors remained {{1}} after the sudden collapse, withdrawing funds at the slightest rumor even from otherwise stable firms.","choices":[["skittish","sanguine","complacent","imperturbable","apathetic"]],"answers":[["skittish"]],"explanation":"Overreaction to slight rumors indicates nervousness and easy alarm. Confidence, calm, complacency, and indifference do not fit.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":865,"targetId":865,"type":"tc","text":"The apparently competitive auction was undermined by {{1}}: bidders secretly agreed to suppress prices and divide the lots among themselves.","choices":[["skullduggery","magnanimity","indolence","circumspection","naivety"]],"answers":[["skullduggery"]],"explanation":"Secret collusion to manipulate prices is dishonest trickery. Prudence alone, laziness, innocence, and generosity do not describe the scheme.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":866,"targetId":866,"type":"tc","text":"The candidate’s invented accusation, delivered in a public speech to ruin her opponent’s reputation, was a clear instance of {{1}}.","choices":[["slander","eulogy","understatement","reparation","equivocation"]],"answers":[["slander"]],"explanation":"A false spoken accusation damaging reputation is slander. Praise, compensation, and ambiguity are not the specified act.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":867,"targetId":867,"type":"tc","text":"The measured difference was {{1}}, amounting to less than one part in a million, although the authors treated it as a dramatic divergence.","choices":[["slight","profound","categorical","ubiquitous","intractable"]],"answers":[["slight"]],"explanation":"The numerical magnitude is extremely small. Profound or categorical exaggerates it; the other adjectives concern distribution or difficulty.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":868,"targetId":868,"type":"tc","text":"The historian’s research was meticulous, but her {{1}} presentation—misnumbered pages, missing labels, and careless citations—obscured that care.","choices":[["slovenly","fastidious","lucid","ornate","systematic"]],"answers":[["slovenly"]],"explanation":"The contrast separates careful research from untidy execution. Slovenly describes careless faults; ornate does not necessarily imply errors.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":869,"targetId":869,"type":"tc","text":"The economy’s response to the stimulus was {{1}}: production barely increased for six months despite forecasts of an immediate surge.","choices":[["sluggish","precipitate","robust","volatile","exuberant"]],"answers":[["sluggish"]],"explanation":"A delayed, weak increase is sluggish. Speed, strength, instability, and enthusiasm are not supported by the described trend.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":870,"targetId":870,"type":"tc","text":"With every other character offstage, the actor delivered a {{1}} that revealed motives the protagonist had concealed in public conversation.","choices":[["soliloquy","dialogue","rebuttal","colloquy","interrogation"]],"answers":[["soliloquy"]],"explanation":"A character speaking thoughts aloud alone delivers a soliloquy. The other forms involve exchange, response, or questioning.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":871,"targetId":871,"type":"tc","text":"The audience was {{1}} after the monotonous lecture, but the chair’s {{2}} aside—a sly joke at his own expense—briefly revived it.","choices":[["somnolent","restive","exultant"],["arch","ponderous","solemn"]],"answers":[["somnolent"],["arch"]],"explanation":"Monotony makes the audience sleepy. A sly, playful aside is arch; ponderous or solemn speech does not describe the joke.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"arch","meaning":"Playfully knowing or teasing"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":872,"targetId":872,"type":"tc","text":"The algorithm was mathematically {{1}}, yet its promotional slogan was merely an {{2}}, compressing the designers’ philosophy into a single memorable line.","choices":[["sophisticated","rudimentary","incoherent"],["apothegm","anomaly","atavism"]],"answers":[["sophisticated"],["apothegm"]],"explanation":"Complex mathematics contrasts with a concise maxim. Apothegm names a short instructive saying; anomaly and atavism concern deviation and recurrence.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"apothegm","meaning":"A brief saying expressing a general insight"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":873,"targetId":873,"type":"tc","text":"The defense relied on {{1}}, using a plausible analogy that concealed a crucial difference; its apparent precision was an {{2}}, not a genuine logical achievement.","choices":[["sophistry","candor","rigor"],["artifice","impediment","apotheosis"]],"answers":[["sophistry"],["artifice"]],"explanation":"Misleading but plausible reasoning is sophistry. Its precision is a deceptive device, or artifice, not an obstacle or culmination.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"artifice","meaning":"A device or trick used to mislead"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":874,"targetId":874,"type":"tc","text":"The critic found the performance {{1}}, although the music was loud; the unvaried rhythm induced drowsiness, making the publicity’s promise of exhilaration seem {{2}}.","choices":[["soporific","scintillating","tempestuous"],["vacuous","prescient","judicious"]],"answers":[["soporific"],["vacuous"]],"explanation":"Monotony can induce sleep despite loudness. The unfulfilled promise is empty, not perceptive or prudent.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"vacuous","meaning":"Empty of meaningful ideas"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":875,"targetId":875,"type":"tc","text":"The proposal was financially {{1}}, supported by conservative projections, but the newcomer’s reputation as an {{2}} made established patrons dismiss it as mere social climbing.","choices":[["sound","quixotic","precarious"],["arriviste","anchorite","apostate"]],"answers":[["sound"],["arriviste"]],"explanation":"Supporting calculations make the plan reliable. Arriviste identifies a socially ambitious newcomer; the dismissal reflects prejudice rather than financial weakness.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"arriviste","meaning":"A recently successful person intent on social advancement"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":876,"targetId":876,"type":"tc","text":"The vegetation was {{1}}, with miles between isolated shrubs; its sudden return after rain was not an {{2}} but the germination of seeds deposited only the previous season.","choices":[["sparse","lush","ubiquitous"],["atavism","improvement","outgrowth"]],"answers":[["sparse"],["atavism"]],"explanation":"Widely separated shrubs indicate sparse growth. The contrast rejects a reappearance of an ancestral condition; recent seeds explain the new growth.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"atavism","meaning":"A return of an ancestral trait"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":877,"targetId":877,"type":"tc","text":"Although the director’s quarters were {{1}}, containing only a bed and desk, the rooms {{2}} to the public gallery were lavishly furnished for visiting donors.","choices":[["spartan","opulent","baroque"],["appurtenant","antithetical","inimical"]],"answers":[["spartan"],["appurtenant"]],"explanation":"Bare quarters are spartan. Appurtenant means attached or belonging as an accessory, describing the gallery’s rooms; contrary or hostile does not fit.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"appurtenant","meaning":"Attached or belonging as an accessory"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":878,"targetId":878,"type":"tc","text":"The argument was {{1}} rather than sound: its neat equations concealed false assumptions, and a careful reader could {{2}} the conclusion without disputing the arithmetic.","choices":[["specious","cogent","transparent"],["refute","corroborate","venerate"]],"answers":[["specious"],["refute"]],"explanation":"Superficial plausibility masking falsity is speciousness. False assumptions permit disproving the conclusion even if calculations are correct.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":879,"targetId":879,"type":"tc","text":"Unlike his father, who saved every coin, the {{1}} soon had to {{2}} the loss of an inheritance exhausted by extravagant purchases.","choices":[["spendthrift","miser","ascetic"],["bemoan","celebrate","underwrite"]],"answers":[["spendthrift"],["bemoan"]],"explanation":"Wasteful spending identifies a spendthrift. The resulting loss is something to lament, not celebrate or financially guarantee.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"bemoan","meaning":"Express sorrow or dissatisfaction over"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":880,"targetId":880,"type":"tc","text":"The scientist’s correspondence became {{1}} after retirement, arriving at irregular intervals; nevertheless, each letter retained the {{2}} humor of a man easily irritated by academic fashions.","choices":[["sporadic","incessant","systematic"],["bilious","guileless","sanguine"]],"answers":[["sporadic"],["bilious"]],"explanation":"Irregular occurrence makes correspondence sporadic. Irritation gives the humor a bad-tempered quality rather than innocence or optimism.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"bilious","meaning":"Bad-tempered and irritable"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":881,"targetId":881,"type":"tc","text":"The signature was {{1}}, traced from another document; the executor’s attempt to {{2}} authority on its basis therefore failed when the original was produced.","choices":[["spurious","authentic","illegible"],["arrogate","relinquish","circumscribe"]],"answers":[["spurious"],["arrogate"]],"explanation":"A traced false signature is spurious. Claiming unauthorized power is arrogating authority, not surrendering or limiting it.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"arrogate","meaning":"Claim power or privileges without authority"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":882,"targetId":882,"type":"tc","text":"The committee chose to {{1}} the donation, regarding acceptance as tacit approval of the donor’s {{2}} destruction of protected habitat.","choices":[["spurn","solicit","allocate"],["wanton","inadvertent","remedial"]],"answers":[["spurn"],["wanton"]],"explanation":"Rejecting with contempt fits spurn. The disapproval concerns reckless destruction rather than an accident or corrective intervention.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"wanton","meaning":"Recklessly disregarding harm or restraint"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":883,"targetId":883,"type":"tc","text":"It would {{1}} years of trust to publish the private letters without consent; even the publisher acknowledged that such a {{2}} might never be repaired.","choices":[["squander","consolidate","legitimize"],["transgression","reprieve","concession"]],"answers":[["squander"],["transgression"]],"explanation":"Unauthorized disclosure would waste accumulated trust. Violating that obligation is a transgression, not a reprieve or concession.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":884,"targetId":884,"type":"tc","text":"A {{1}} supporter of the museum, she continued to contribute during its leanest years, while less loyal patrons withdrew the {{2}} of enthusiasm they had displayed during its fashionable opening.","choices":[["stalwart","fickle","perfunctory"],["veneer","apotheosis","rigor"]],"answers":[["stalwart"],["veneer"]],"explanation":"Continuing in adversity demonstrates stalwart loyalty. The others’ enthusiasm proves an outward surface, not a culmination or exacting method.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"veneer","meaning":"An outward covering that conceals the underlying reality"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":885,"targetId":885,"type":"tc","text":"Her commitment remained {{1}} through repeated defeats; rather than diminishing, her determination seemed to {{2}} with each new obstacle.","choices":[["steadfast","mercurial","tentative"],["wax","wane","dissipate"]],"answers":[["steadfast"],["wax"]],"explanation":"Unwavering commitment is steadfast. Rather than diminishing requires growth in determination, expressed by wax.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"wax","meaning":"Grow in strength or intensity"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":886,"targetId":886,"type":"tc","text":"The principal’s {{1}} rebuke surprised students used to indulgence, but its {{2}} was deliberate: she believed mild language would {{3}} the seriousness of the misconduct.","choices":[["stern","genial","diffident"],["asperity","levity","opacity"],["understate","exacerbate","authenticate"]],"answers":[["stern"],["asperity"],["understate"]],"explanation":"A severe rebuke is stern; deliberate harshness is asperity. Mild wording would make misconduct seem less serious, or understate it, rather than worsen or authenticate it.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"asperity","meaning":"Harshness in speech or manner"},{"word":"understate","meaning":"Describe as less important or serious than it is"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":887,"targetId":887,"type":"tc","text":"Public campaigns that {{1}} addiction can be {{2}} to recovery: fear of condemnation may {{3}} people who would otherwise seek help.","choices":[["stigmatize","normalize","demystify"],["inimical","salutary","appurtenant"],["unnerve","embolden","reassure"]],"answers":[["stigmatize"],["inimical"],["unnerve"]],"explanation":"Marking addiction as shameful is stigmatizing it. Deterring help is harmful to recovery. Fear shakes confidence, completing the causal chain with unnerve.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"unnerve","meaning":"Shake someone’s confidence or composure"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":888,"targetId":888,"type":"tc","text":"The patron’s {{1}} support barely paid for materials, but he demanded {{2}} praise; the artist refused to offer such {{3}} acclaim for so little assistance.","choices":[["stinting","munificent","lavish"],["fulsome","qualified","muted"],["extravagant","measured","tacit"]],"answers":[["stinting"],["fulsome"],["extravagant"]],"explanation":"Barely adequate funding is stinting. The contrast requires excessive praise: fulsome and extravagant. The other choices describe limited or unspoken praise.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"fulsome","meaning":"Excessive and insincere in praise"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":889,"targetId":889,"type":"tc","text":"The expedition leader remained {{1}} during the ordeal, never complaining, though her journal later revealed intense {{2}}; her outward calm was therefore evidence of restraint, not {{3}}.","choices":[["stoic","petulant","vociferous"],["vexation","delectation","complacency"],["indifference","discipline","fortitude"]],"answers":[["stoic"],["vexation"],["indifference"]],"explanation":"Enduring without complaint is stoic. Hidden annoyance contrasts with composure. That distress rules out indifference while supporting discipline and fortitude.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":890,"targetId":890,"type":"tc","text":"His {{1}} face gave no hint of emotion, so reporters mistook his silence for {{2}}; in fact, his private notes recorded {{3}} delight at the acquittal.","choices":[["stolid","radiant","contorted"],["apathy","elation","fervor"],["unalloyed","tepid","feigned"]],"answers":[["stolid"],["apathy"],["unalloyed"]],"explanation":"An unemotional face is stolid. Reporters infer apathy. The revealed contrast is genuine, pure delight, not weak or simulated joy.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":891,"targetId":891,"type":"se","text":"The arrangement intended to unite the departments instead generated {{1}}, with bitter disputes over resources replacing their former cooperation.","choices":[["strife","discord","deference","camaraderie","compliance","reticence"]],"answers":[["strife","discord"]],"explanation":"Strife and discord both describe bitter conflict. Disputes replacing cooperation rule out harmony, obedience, or mere silence.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"discord","meaning":"Bitter disagreement"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":892,"targetId":892,"type":"se","text":"The laboratory’s {{1}} standards allowed no deviation from the protocol and required every measurement to be independently replicated.","choices":[["stringent","exacting","permissive","arbitrary","provisional","antiquated"]],"answers":[["stringent","exacting"]],"explanation":"Stringent and exacting convey strict, demanding standards. The detail establishes rigor, not random choice, temporary status, or age.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":893,"targetId":893,"type":"se","text":"The ranking is explicitly {{1}}, reflecting each critic’s own preferences rather than any shared and independently measurable criterion.","choices":[["subjective","personal","empirical","universal","impartial","definitive"]],"answers":[["subjective","personal"]],"explanation":"Subjective and personal both locate the judgment in individual preference. The sentence rejects objective or universally applicable measurement.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"personal","meaning":"Arising from an individual’s own perspective"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":894,"targetId":894,"type":"se","text":"In the architect’s scheme, ornament was {{1}} to function: any decorative element that impaired use was removed.","choices":[["subordinate","secondary","paramount","extraneous","antithetical","equivalent"]],"answers":[["subordinate","secondary"]],"explanation":"Subordinate and secondary place ornament below function in importance. Ornament is not necessarily irrelevant or opposed to function; compatible ornament remains.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"secondary","meaning":"Of less importance or rank"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":895,"targetId":895,"type":"se","text":"The adviser was so {{1}} that he endorsed every demand of the ruler, however unreasonable, and never ventured a contrary opinion.","choices":[["subservient","servile","conciliatory","autonomous","judicious","steadfast"]],"answers":[["subservient","servile"]],"explanation":"Subservient and servile capture excessive obedience. Agreement with every unreasonable demand exceeds reconciliation or loyalty and excludes independent judgment.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"servile","meaning":"Excessively submissive toward authority"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":896,"targetId":896,"type":"se","text":"Once the reassuring evidence was published, public anxiety began to {{1}}, and the emergency hotline received steadily fewer calls.","choices":[["subside","abate","proliferate","recur","crystallize","persist"]],"answers":[["subside","abate"]],"explanation":"Subside and abate mean decrease in intensity. Declining calls support diminishing anxiety, not spread, recurrence, or persistence.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":897,"targetId":897,"type":"se","text":"Before including the allegation in her report, the journalist sought records that could {{1}} it with independently checkable evidence.","choices":[["substantiate","verify","embroider","disseminate","attenuate","obfuscate"]],"answers":[["substantiate","verify"]],"explanation":"Substantiate and verify concern establishing evidential support or truth. Embellishing, spreading, weakening, or obscuring is different from checking.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"verify","meaning":"Establish the truth through evidence"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":898,"targetId":898,"type":"se","text":"The proposed category would {{1}} both ceremonial and practical objects, bringing previously separate collections under one heading.","choices":[["subsume","encompass","segregate","replicate","displace","exclude"]],"answers":[["subsume","encompass"]],"explanation":"Subsume and encompass mean include within a larger whole. The shared heading combines categories rather than separating or excluding them.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"encompass","meaning":"Include within a larger whole"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":899,"targetId":899,"type":"se","text":"The historian’s account is unusually {{1}}, distinguishing shades of loyalty within each faction instead of assigning everyone to two rigid camps.","choices":[["subtle","nuanced","categorical","perfunctory","reductive","dogmatic"]],"answers":[["subtle","nuanced"]],"explanation":"Subtle and nuanced describe attention to fine distinctions. Rigid categorization and reduction are what the account avoids.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"nuanced","meaning":"Marked by fine distinctions"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":900,"targetId":900,"type":"se","text":"By quietly bribing its inspectors, the cartel hoped to {{1}} the regulatory system from within, eroding its capacity to enforce its own rules.","choices":[["subvert","destabilize","legitimize","codify","consolidate","replicate"]],"answers":[["subvert","destabilize"]],"explanation":"Subvert and destabilize express weakening the system. Bribery undermines enforcement rather than legitimizing or strengthening it.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"destabilize","meaning":"Weaken the stability of a system"}],"section":18,"initial":"s"},{"id":901,"targetId":901,"type":"tc","text":"The review was {{1}} despite its length: it described the book’s cover and typography but never examined its central argument.","choices":[["superficial","exhaustive","trenchant","penetrating","contentious"]],"answers":[["superficial"]],"explanation":"Ignoring substance while describing appearances makes the review superficial. Length does not make it exhaustive or perceptive.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":902,"targetId":902,"type":"tc","text":"Once the automated alarm had been installed, the separate bell became {{1}}, adding no warning that the new system did not already provide.","choices":[["superfluous","indispensable","complementary","defective","ominous"]],"answers":[["superfluous"]],"explanation":"The bell adds nothing needed, making it superfluous. It need not be defective; complementary would imply an additional useful function.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":903,"targetId":903,"type":"tc","text":"The revised manual will {{1}} the previous edition, which employees have been instructed to discard once the replacement arrives.","choices":[["supersede","vindicate","epitomize","abridge","corroborate"]],"answers":[["supersede"]],"explanation":"Discarding the old edition for a replacement means it is superseded. Abridging shortens it; corroborating supports it.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":904,"targetId":904,"type":"tc","text":"The new crop was intended to supplement existing varieties, but its higher yield led farmers to {{1}} them entirely.","choices":[["supplant","propagate","diversify","preserve","fortify"]],"answers":[["supplant"]],"explanation":"The contrast with supplement and the word entirely require replacement, or supplanting, rather than preserving the old varieties.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":905,"targetId":905,"type":"tc","text":"The material had to remain {{1}} in cold weather, since a rigid seal would crack when the machine’s parts moved.","choices":[["supple","brittle","porous","opaque","abrasive"]],"answers":[["supple"]],"explanation":"Supple supplies the required flexibility. Brittleness creates the problem; the other properties do not address bending.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":906,"targetId":906,"type":"tc","text":"Having exhausted every legal avenue, the petitioner could only {{1}} the governor for mercy, kneeling as she presented her appeal.","choices":[["supplicate","censure","adjudicate","indemnify","beguile"]],"answers":[["supplicate"]],"explanation":"The humble plea is supplication. Criticizing, judging, compensating, or charming deceptively does not describe that act.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":907,"targetId":907,"type":"tc","text":"The expedition succeeded because the team could {{1}} obstacles that earlier travelers had considered insuperable.","choices":[["surmount","perpetuate","magnify","catalogue","replicate"]],"answers":[["surmount"]],"explanation":"Success against supposedly insuperable obstacles requires overcoming them. Listing, repeating, or enlarging obstacles does not explain success.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":908,"targetId":908,"type":"tc","text":"The copying was {{1}}: she photographed the manuscript only when the archivist turned away and concealed the camera whenever anyone approached.","choices":[["surreptitious","ostentatious","authorized","perfunctory","indiscriminate"]],"answers":[["surreptitious"]],"explanation":"Concealment to avoid notice is surreptitious. The evidence concerns secrecy, not permission, display, or randomness.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":909,"targetId":909,"type":"tc","text":"The data became {{1}} when auditors discovered that several supposedly independent observations had been copied from the same notebook.","choices":[["suspect","definitive","representative","exemplary","incontrovertible"]],"answers":[["suspect"]],"explanation":"False independence makes the data questionable, or suspect, rather than certain or exemplary.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":910,"targetId":910,"type":"tc","text":"The scheme was designed to {{1}} retirees out of their savings by selling shares in a company that existed only on paper.","choices":[["swindle","absolve","reimburse","dissuade","vindicate"]],"answers":[["swindle"]],"explanation":"Taking savings by deception is swindling. The other verbs involve forgiveness, repayment, persuasion, or justification.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":911,"targetId":911,"type":"tc","text":"Rather than reproduce thousands of archive entries, the curator supplied a {{1}} chart showing the collection’s broad development at a glance.","choices":[["synoptic","exhaustive","fragmentary","digressive","recondite"]],"answers":[["synoptic"]],"explanation":"An at-a-glance overview is synoptic. Exhaustiveness would retain every detail; fragmentation would lose the coherent overview.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"s"},{"id":912,"targetId":912,"type":"tc","text":"No rule barred discussion of salaries, yet employees observed a {{1}} agreement to avoid the subject, understanding the convention without ever stating it.","choices":[["tacit","statutory","explicit","provisional","coercive"]],"answers":[["tacit"]],"explanation":"An understood but unstated agreement is tacit. Neither a law nor an explicit statement establishes this convention.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":913,"targetId":913,"type":"tc","text":"The normally {{1}} biographer astonished her hosts by talking uninterruptedly for an hour about the newly discovered diary.","choices":[["taciturn","voluble","effusive","gregarious","didactic"]],"answers":[["taciturn"]],"explanation":"Surprise requires a contrast between habitual quiet and unusual talkativeness. Taciturn supplies it; didactic concerns purpose rather than amount of speech.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":914,"targetId":914,"type":"tc","text":"Correcting the donor’s mistake without embarrassing him required {{1}}; a blunt public contradiction might have ended his support.","choices":[["tact","temerity","pedantry","guilelessness","indifference"]],"answers":[["tact"]],"explanation":"Sensitive handling requires tact. Boldness or pedantry could increase embarrassment; innocence and indifference do not provide the skill.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":915,"targetId":915,"type":"tc","text":"The digression about the novelist’s garden was {{1}} to the discussion of her political theory, sharing only a distant connection with the argument.","choices":[["tangential","integral","germane","antithetical","conclusive"]],"answers":[["tangential"]],"explanation":"A distant connection is tangential. The digression is neither central nor directly relevant, and opposition is not stated.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":916,"targetId":916,"type":"tc","text":"After years of abstract promises, residents wanted {{1}} evidence of improvement: functioning wells and repaired roads rather than another policy statement.","choices":[["tangible","hypothetical","equivocal","anecdotal","symbolic"]],"answers":[["tangible"]],"explanation":"Concrete observable results are tangible. The contrast rejects merely hypothetical or symbolic promises.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":917,"targetId":917,"type":"tc","text":"The fragment was {{1}}, revealing just enough of the lost poem to suggest its brilliance while leaving its conclusion permanently inaccessible.","choices":[["tantalizing","definitive","soporific","commonplace","exhaustive"]],"answers":[["tantalizing"]],"explanation":"A glimpse of something desirable that remains inaccessible is tantalizing. The fragment cannot be definitive or exhaustive.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":918,"targetId":918,"type":"tc","text":"Although the memorandum never used the word rejection, postponing the application indefinitely was {{1}} to refusing it.","choices":[["tantamount","incidental","antithetical","subordinate","preliminary"]],"answers":[["tantamount"]],"explanation":"Indefinite postponement has the same practical effect as refusal. Tantamount expresses that equivalence.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":919,"targetId":919,"type":"tc","text":"The discovery of fabricated interviews threatened to {{1}} the journalist’s reputation, previously founded on unusually careful verification.","choices":[["tarnish","vindicate","consolidate","enhance","epitomize"]],"answers":[["tarnish"]],"explanation":"Fabrication damages a reputation for accuracy. Tarnish expresses the harm; the other choices support or exemplify it.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":920,"targetId":920,"type":"tc","text":"Even readers sympathetic to the thesis found the appendix {{1}}, as it repeated the same calculation with negligible changes for eighty pages.","choices":[["tedious","illuminating","succinct","provocative","scintillating"]],"answers":[["tedious"]],"explanation":"Lengthy repetition is tiresome. Sympathy with the argument does not make the appendix brief, revealing, or lively.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":921,"targetId":921,"type":"tc","text":"The apprentice’s {{1}} in correcting the celebrated master offended the audience, but the master’s response was {{2}}: she praised the correction’s accuracy.","choices":[["temerity","reticence","deference"],["approbatory","bilious","scathing"]],"answers":[["temerity"],["approbatory"]],"explanation":"Presumptuous boldness is temerity. Praise makes the response approving, contrasting with the audience’s offense.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"approbatory","meaning":"Expressing favorable judgment"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":922,"targetId":922,"type":"tc","text":"The editor sought to {{1}} the essay’s hostility without making it {{2}}; she wanted criticism to retain its force while losing personal insults.","choices":[["temper","intensify","disguise"],["anodyne","trenchant","incisive"]],"answers":[["temper"],["anodyne"]],"explanation":"Temper means moderate. The criticism should remain forceful rather than become entirely inoffensive, or anodyne.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"anodyne","meaning":"Soothing or unlikely to cause offense"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":923,"targetId":923,"type":"tc","text":"Their {{1}} collaboration alternated between inspired agreement and furious quarrels; observers calling it consistently harmonious mistook a temporary truce for an enduring {{2}}.","choices":[["tempestuous","equable","perfunctory"],["accord","recrimination","rupture"]],"answers":[["tempestuous"],["accord"]],"explanation":"Emotional turbulence makes the collaboration tempestuous. The error is treating a short truce as lasting agreement, not blame or rupture.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"accord","meaning":"Agreement or harmony"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":924,"targetId":924,"type":"tc","text":"The historian separated {{1}} authority from spiritual authority, arguing that control over taxes reflected earthly power rather than a {{2}} claim to divine wisdom.","choices":[["temporal","transcendent","ethereal"],["sacerdotal","secular","commercial"]],"answers":[["temporal"],["sacerdotal"]],"explanation":"Temporal means worldly here. Sacerdotal concerns priestly authority; secular and commercial remain earthly and break the contrast.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"sacerdotal","meaning":"Relating to priests or religious office"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":925,"targetId":925,"type":"tc","text":"The theory remained {{1}} despite the anomaly, since a minor adjustment explained it; critics proclaiming its total collapse had been {{2}}.","choices":[["tenable","untenable","incontrovertible"],["precipitate","circumspect","prescient"]],"answers":[["tenable"],["precipitate"]],"explanation":"The adjustment keeps the theory defensible without making it indisputable. Declaring collapse prematurely is precipitate, not careful or foresighted.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":926,"targetId":926,"type":"tc","text":"The article was {{1}}, selecting only evidence favorable to its position, but its calm prose gave it a misleading {{2}} of impartiality.","choices":[["tendentious","eclectic","equitable"],["veneer","refutation","absence"]],"answers":[["tendentious"],["veneer"]],"explanation":"Selective presentation is biased, or tendentious. The style offers only an outward appearance of impartiality, a veneer.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"veneer","meaning":"An outward covering that conceals the underlying reality"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":927,"targetId":927,"type":"tc","text":"The agreement was {{1}}, subject to revision after further testing; treating it as {{2}} would ignore its explicit expiration clause.","choices":[["tentative","irrevocable","categorical"],["immutable","provisional","contingent"]],"answers":[["tentative"],["immutable"]],"explanation":"Possible revision makes it tentative. Calling it unchangeable would contradict that condition, while provisional and contingent acknowledge it.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":928,"targetId":928,"type":"tc","text":"The proposed connection was {{1}}, resting on a single ambiguous letter; corroborating records would be needed to {{2}} it.","choices":[["tenuous","robust","conclusive"],["substantiate","attenuate","obfuscate"]],"answers":[["tenuous"],["substantiate"]],"explanation":"Weak evidence creates a tenuous connection. Corroboration would provide support, not weaken or obscure it.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":929,"targetId":929,"type":"tc","text":"The committee’s {{1}} endorsement disappointed the inventor: members expressed little enthusiasm, although their comments were not openly {{2}}.","choices":[["tepid","fervent","effusive"],["hostile","approbatory","guarded"]],"answers":[["tepid"],["hostile"]],"explanation":"Little enthusiasm makes the support tepid. The concession distinguishes lukewarm approval from outright hostility, not from approval itself.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"hostile","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":930,"targetId":930,"type":"tc","text":"The director’s {{1}} reply contained only three words; it resembled an {{2}} in its compressed wisdom, though its brevity initially seemed brusque.","choices":[["terse","verbose","circuitous"],["apothegm","encomium","tirade"]],"answers":[["terse"],["apothegm"]],"explanation":"Extreme brevity is terse. Compressed general wisdom resembles an apothegm, not necessarily praise or an angry speech.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"apothegm","meaning":"A brief saying expressing a general insight"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":931,"targetId":931,"type":"tc","text":"The inspection was {{1}}, extending to every compartment, and the report was equally {{2}}, recording even defects too small to affect operation.","choices":[["thorough","cursory","piecemeal"],["meticulous","desultory","laconic"]],"answers":[["thorough"],["meticulous"]],"explanation":"Every compartment establishes completeness. Careful recording of tiny details makes the report meticulous, not aimless or merely concise.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":932,"targetId":932,"type":"tc","text":"The witness was {{1}} on entering the courtroom, but the judge’s reassuring manner gradually {{2}} her fear.","choices":[["timorous","brazen","imperturbable"],["assuaged","exacerbated","vindicated"]],"answers":[["timorous"],["assuaged"]],"explanation":"Timorous means fearful. Reassurance reduces or assuages fear rather than worsening or justifying it.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"assuaged","meaning":"Made less intense or distressing"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":933,"targetId":933,"type":"tc","text":"What began as a routine correction became a {{1}}, a prolonged denunciation whose {{2}} surprised colleagues accustomed to the editor’s mild voice.","choices":[["tirade","elegy","panegyric"],["asperity","brevity","equanimity"]],"answers":[["tirade"],["asperity"]],"explanation":"A prolonged denunciation is a tirade. Harshness, or asperity, contrasts with mildness; brevity and composure contradict the description.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"asperity","meaning":"Harshness in speech or manner"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":934,"targetId":934,"type":"tc","text":"The city emerged from winter {{1}} as festivals filled its empty streets; residents who had {{2}} months of inactivity now complained of excessive bustle.","choices":[["torpor","fervor","discord"],["bemoaned","celebrated","prolonged"]],"answers":[["torpor"],["bemoaned"]],"explanation":"Winter inactivity is torpor. The irony concerns residents who lamented inactivity now disliking the opposite condition.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"bemoaned","meaning":"Expressed regret or discontent about"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":935,"targetId":935,"type":"tc","text":"The legal reasoning was {{1}}, reaching its conclusion through a maze of exceptions; the judge’s summary, by contrast, was {{2}} enough for nonspecialists to follow.","choices":[["tortuous","straightforward","fallacious"],["lucid","recondite","elliptical"]],"answers":[["tortuous"],["lucid"]],"explanation":"A maze makes reasoning convoluted, not necessarily false. The accessible contrasting summary is lucid rather than obscure.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":936,"targetId":936,"type":"tc","text":"The company continued to {{1}} the device as revolutionary, although tests found its benefits {{2}}; the discrepancy made the advertising appear {{3}}.","choices":[["tout","deprecate","withdraw"],["negligible","prodigious","transformative"],["mendacious","candid","understated"]],"answers":[["tout"],["negligible"],["mendacious"]],"explanation":"Tout means promote enthusiastically. Tiny benefits conflict with revolutionary claims, making the advertisement dishonest rather than candid or modest.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"mendacious","meaning":"Dishonest or untruthful"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":937,"targetId":937,"type":"tc","text":"The animal proved {{1}} once handled gently, so its earlier resistance had been {{2}} rather than habitual; the trainer abandoned the idea that it was intrinsically {{3}}.","choices":[["tractable","recalcitrant","feral"],["situational","immutable","inexplicable"],["unruly","docile","manageable"]],"answers":[["tractable"],["situational"],["unruly"]],"explanation":"Cooperation shows tractability. Changed handling explains resistance as situational, undermining a diagnosis of inherent unruliness.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"situational","meaning":"Arising from particular circumstances"},{"word":"unruly","meaning":"Resisting discipline or control"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":938,"targetId":938,"type":"tc","text":"The bay looked {{1}} from shore, but the sailor’s confidence was {{2}}: beneath the smooth surface, dangerous currents made careless navigation {{3}}.","choices":[["tranquil","turbulent","tempestuous"],["misplaced","warranted","prescient"],["perilous","salutary","effortless"]],"answers":[["tranquil"],["misplaced"],["perilous"]],"explanation":"Calm appearance is tranquil. Hidden danger makes confidence misplaced and careless travel perilous; surface calm does not guarantee safety.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"misplaced","meaning":"Directed or applied inappropriately"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":939,"targetId":939,"type":"tc","text":"The novelist hoped to {{1}} her genre’s conventions, but her earliest drafts merely {{2}} them; only the final book achieved the {{3}} she sought.","choices":[["transcend","codify","reinforce"],["replicated","subverted","discarded"],["originality","conformity","redundancy"]],"answers":[["transcend"],["replicated"],["originality"]],"explanation":"The aim is to go beyond convention. Early drafts merely copied it; the contrasting final achievement is originality.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"replicated","meaning":"PENDING"},{"word":"originality","meaning":"The quality of being new and independently conceived"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":940,"targetId":940,"type":"tc","text":"The audit exposed a serious {{1}}, not a harmless oversight: the accountant had {{2}} authority to redirect funds and devised an {{3}} to conceal the transfers.","choices":[["transgression","reprieve","concession"],["arrogated","relinquished","circumscribed"],["artifice","apothegm","accord"]],"answers":[["transgression"],["arrogated"],["artifice"]],"explanation":"The diversion violates rules. Arrogated means claimed without authorization; concealing it with a trick requires artifice.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"arrogated","meaning":"Claimed without rightful authority"},{"word":"artifice","meaning":"A device or trick used to mislead"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":941,"targetId":941,"type":"se","text":"The critic dismissed the fashion as {{1}}, predicting that its sudden popularity would disappear as quickly as it had arisen.","choices":[["transient","fleeting","entrenched","perennial","salutary","eclectic"]],"answers":[["transient","fleeting"]],"explanation":"Transient and fleeting mean short-lived. The prediction concerns duration rather than benefit or stylistic variety.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"fleeting","meaning":"Passing very quickly"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":942,"targetId":942,"type":"se","text":"Because the disturbance was {{1}}, lasting only a few seconds, engineers sought a temporary adjustment rather than a permanent redesign.","choices":[["transitory","ephemeral","intractable","incessant","endemic","irreversible"]],"answers":[["transitory","ephemeral"]],"explanation":"Transitory and ephemeral describe brief duration. The seconds-long disturbance is not persistent or necessarily irreversible.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":943,"targetId":943,"type":"se","text":"The scholar’s {{1}} on the history of one medieval tax was a sustained, book-length investigation rather than a brief survey of fiscal policy.","choices":[["treatise","monograph","epigram","anthology","catalogue","digression"]],"answers":[["treatise","monograph"]],"explanation":"Treatise and monograph both describe the detailed scholarly work. A single sustained investigation is neither a short saying nor an assorted collection.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"monograph","meaning":"A detailed scholarly work on one topic"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":944,"targetId":944,"type":"se","text":"Her {{1}} analysis cut through the impressive terminology to identify precisely the assumption on which the entire theory depended.","choices":[["trenchant","incisive","perfunctory","oblique","diffuse","deferential"]],"answers":[["trenchant","incisive"]],"explanation":"Trenchant and incisive convey sharp perception and clarity. Identifying the key assumption contrasts with superficial, indirect, or sprawling treatment.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":945,"targetId":945,"type":"se","text":"The clerical discrepancy was {{1}}, affecting neither the result nor anyone’s entitlement, so the panel declined to reopen the case.","choices":[["trifling","inconsequential","ominous","intractable","germane","systematic"]],"answers":[["trifling","inconsequential"]],"explanation":"Trifling and inconsequential mean too minor to matter. The absence of effects, not relevance or frequency, explains the decision.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"inconsequential","meaning":"Too minor to have significant effects"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":946,"targetId":946,"type":"se","text":"Relative to the bridge’s total cost, the inspection price was {{1}}, amounting to less than one hundredth of one percent.","choices":[["trivial","negligible","exorbitant","commensurate","inestimable","prohibitive"]],"answers":[["trivial","negligible"]],"explanation":"Trivial and negligible characterize the tiny relative cost. The numeric comparison excludes excessive or incalculable expense.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":947,"targetId":947,"type":"se","text":"The delegate’s {{1}} response turned a routine disagreement into confrontation, as he threatened retaliation before anyone proposed a compromise.","choices":[["truculent","belligerent","conciliatory","diffident","imperturbable","equivocal"]],"answers":[["truculent","belligerent"]],"explanation":"Truculent and belligerent denote aggressive hostility. Threats support neither conciliation nor calm, shyness, or ambiguity.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":948,"targetId":948,"type":"se","text":"The years following the collapse were {{1}}, marked by uprisings, abrupt changes of government, and the breakdown of ordinary administration.","choices":[["turbulent","tumultuous","quiescent","uneventful","prosperous","incremental"]],"answers":[["turbulent","tumultuous"]],"explanation":"Turbulent and tumultuous describe disorder and upheaval. Uprisings and sudden changes exclude quiet or gradual development.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"tumultuous","meaning":"Marked by disorder or upheaval"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":949,"targetId":949,"type":"se","text":"The inquiry revealed {{1}} at the institution’s core: officials knowingly sold essential supplies while those in their care went hungry.","choices":[["turpitude","depravity","incompetence","parsimony","naivety","dissent"]],"answers":[["turpitude","depravity"]],"explanation":"Turpitude and depravity identify grave moral corruption. Deliberate exploitation exceeds incompetence or thrift and contradicts innocence.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"depravity","meaning":"Profound moral corruption"}],"section":19,"initial":"t"},{"id":950,"targetId":950,"type":"se","text":"Once a rarity confined to specialist laboratories, the sensor is now {{1}}, appearing in virtually every household appliance.","choices":[["ubiquitous","omnipresent","obsolete","esoteric","sporadic","redundant"]],"answers":[["ubiquitous","omnipresent"]],"explanation":"Ubiquitous and omnipresent express presence everywhere. The contrast concerns rarity, not age or usefulness.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":19,"initial":"u"},{"id":951,"targetId":951,"type":"tc","text":"The composer took {{1}} at the suggestion that her work merely imitated her teacher’s, replying indignantly that the resemblance was superficial.","choices":[["umbrage","delight","solace","precedence","credence"]],"answers":[["umbrage"]],"explanation":"Her indignant response shows offense or resentment, which is umbrage. Delight and solace are positive; the other nouns do not express her reaction.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":952,"targetId":952,"type":"tc","text":"Their relief was {{1}}: with every passenger safe and the vessel undamaged, no lingering concern qualified their happiness.","choices":[["unalloyed","ambivalent","tentative","feigned","muted"]],"answers":[["unalloyed"]],"explanation":"Nothing mixes with or limits the happiness, making it unalloyed. Ambivalence or hesitation would introduce the concerns explicitly absent.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":953,"targetId":953,"type":"tc","text":"By selling the same product below its rival’s cost, the firm hoped to {{1}} the rival’s prices and capture its customers.","choices":[["undercut","standardize","vindicate","replicate","stabilize"]],"answers":[["undercut"]],"explanation":"Offering a lower price is undercutting. Matching, justifying, standardizing, or stabilizing prices would not create the specified advantage.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":954,"targetId":954,"type":"tc","text":"Repeated small exceptions can {{1}} a rule’s authority even when no single exception seems serious enough to challenge it openly.","choices":[["undermine","consolidate","codify","epitomize","authenticate"]],"answers":[["undermine"]],"explanation":"The cumulative erosion is gradual weakening, or undermining. The other choices strengthen, formulate, exemplify, or validate authority.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":955,"targetId":955,"type":"tc","text":"The author repeats the same image in the final paragraph to {{1}} the connection between private memory and public history.","choices":[["underscore","obscure","sever","qualify","discredit"]],"answers":[["underscore"]],"explanation":"Deliberate repetition emphasizes the connection. The sentence supplies no evidence that the author wishes to hide, break, restrict, or attack it.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":956,"targetId":956,"type":"tc","text":"The memorial was deliberately {{1}}: a small plaque and an unadorned stone conveyed remembrance without theatrical display.","choices":[["understated","ostentatious","bombastic","ornate","flamboyant"]],"answers":[["understated"]],"explanation":"Restrained expression without showiness is understated. Every alternative involves conspicuous elaboration or display.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":957,"targetId":957,"type":"tc","text":"The principle was intended to be {{1}}, applying equally to every resident regardless of occupation, income, or place of birth.","choices":[["universal","contingent","parochial","provisional","esoteric"]],"answers":[["universal"]],"explanation":"Application to everyone is universal. Conditionality, narrow locality, temporary status, and specialized knowledge are different limitations.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":958,"targetId":958,"type":"tc","text":"The decision was {{1}} in the court’s history: researchers found no earlier case in which an equivalent remedy had been granted.","choices":[["unprecedented","customary","anachronistic","derivative","inevitable"]],"answers":[["unprecedented"]],"explanation":"The lack of any earlier instance makes the remedy unprecedented. It is therefore not customary or simply copied; inevitability is not established.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":959,"targetId":959,"type":"tc","text":"The dealer was {{1}}, concealing defects he knew would endanger buyers whenever disclosure might reduce his profits.","choices":[["unscrupulous","punctilious","guileless","diffident","munificent"]],"answers":[["unscrupulous"]],"explanation":"Knowingly risking buyers’ safety for profit shows absence of moral principles. Care, innocence, shyness, and generosity do not fit.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":960,"targetId":960,"type":"tc","text":"Even her supporters considered the minister’s laughter {{1}} during the memorial, where solemnity rather than amusement was expected.","choices":[["unseemly","decorous","opportune","salutary","inevitable"]],"answers":[["unseemly"]],"explanation":"Laughter violates the occasion’s expectations, making it improper or unseemly. The objection concerns appropriateness, not inevitability.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":961,"targetId":961,"type":"tc","text":"The supervisor chose to {{1}} the technician for deliberately ignoring the safety checks, delivering a severe reprimand before the next shift.","choices":[["upbraid","exonerate","commend","placate","indemnify"]],"answers":[["upbraid"]],"explanation":"A severe reprimand is upbraiding. Clearing blame, praising, soothing, and compensating are inconsistent with the stated action.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":962,"targetId":962,"type":"tc","text":"His {{1}} handling of the awkward introduction put both guests at ease: he acknowledged their disagreement without a trace of discourtesy.","choices":[["urbane","gauche","boorish","strident","impetuous"]],"answers":[["urbane"]],"explanation":"Polished courtesy in a delicate social situation is urbane. The other traits would undermine that graceful handling.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":963,"targetId":963,"type":"tc","text":"The chairs were strictly {{1}}, chosen for durability and ease of stacking rather than for elegance or ornament.","choices":[["utilitarian","decorative","opulent","whimsical","baroque"]],"answers":[["utilitarian"]],"explanation":"The selection prioritizes practical function. Utilitarian fits, whereas the alternatives foreground appearance, luxury, or fancy.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":964,"targetId":964,"type":"tc","text":"The proposed reconciliation was {{1}} impossible: neither party recognized the other’s existence, much less its right to negotiate.","choices":[["utterly","marginally","intermittently","approximately","partially"]],"answers":[["utterly"]],"explanation":"The emphatic explanation rules out even preliminary negotiation. Utterly supplies total impossibility, unlike qualified or occasional impossibility.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"u"},{"id":965,"targetId":965,"type":"tc","text":"Asked to choose a site, the committee continued to {{1}}, endorsing the riverfront one week and the hilltop the next without reaching a final decision.","choices":[["vacillate","concur","persevere","capitulate","expedite"]],"answers":[["vacillate"]],"explanation":"Alternating repeatedly between options is vacillation. It is not agreement, firm persistence, surrender, or acceleration.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":966,"targetId":966,"type":"tc","text":"The award recognized the firefighter’s {{1}}, specifically her decision to enter the unstable building despite knowing that it could collapse.","choices":[["valor","circumspection","complacency","equanimity","acumen"]],"answers":[["valor"]],"explanation":"Facing a known danger to help others demonstrates bravery. Calm or judgment might accompany it, but the cited action specifically recognizes courage.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":967,"targetId":967,"type":"tc","text":"The challenger did not merely edge out the champion; she managed to {{1}} him, winning every round by an overwhelming margin.","choices":[["vanquish","emulate","appease","indemnify","circumvent"]],"answers":[["vanquish"]],"explanation":"Decisive defeat is vanquishing. Imitation, appeasement, compensation, and avoidance do not capture the overwhelming victory.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":968,"targetId":968,"type":"tc","text":"Beneath its polished language, the speech was {{1}}, offering familiar slogans but no developed ideas or substantive proposals.","choices":[["vapid","trenchant","provocative","erudite","cogent"]],"answers":[["vapid"]],"explanation":"Empty slogans without substance make the speech vapid. Polish alone does not provide perception, learning, or reasoning.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":969,"targetId":969,"type":"tc","text":"The official was openly {{1}}: applicants learned that a payment to his private account reliably secured an otherwise unavailable permit.","choices":[["venal","incorruptible","naive","diffident","parsimonious"]],"answers":[["venal"]],"explanation":"Willingness to exchange official favors for bribes is venality. Thrift, innocence, or shyness does not name that corruption.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":970,"targetId":970,"type":"tc","text":"Although later scholars rejected many of her conclusions, they continued to {{1}} the pioneering researcher for the courage and care of her investigations.","choices":[["venerate","vilify","patronize","disparage","censure"]],"answers":[["venerate"]],"explanation":"Rejection of conclusions contrasts with enduring deep respect for her work. Venerate fits; the other choices diminish or condemn her.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":971,"targetId":971,"type":"tc","text":"Doubts about the witness’s {{1}} persisted until recordings confirmed every disputed detail; the resulting {{2}} cleared him of the charge of lying.","choices":[["veracity","eloquence","reticence"],["exoneration","indictment","recrimination"]],"answers":[["veracity"],["exoneration"]],"explanation":"Recordings establish truthfulness, not speaking style. Clearing a false accusation is exoneration, the opposite of indictment or renewed blame.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"exoneration","meaning":"The clearing of someone from blame"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":972,"targetId":972,"type":"tc","text":"The report was {{1}}, repeating each conclusion in several elaborate formulations; its editor removed the {{2}} without sacrificing any distinct finding.","choices":[["verbose","terse","elliptical"],["redundancy","substance","coherence"]],"answers":[["verbose"],["redundancy"]],"explanation":"Excess words and repeated formulations make the report verbose. Removing unnecessary repetition preserves meaning, unlike removing substance or coherence.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"redundancy","meaning":"Unnecessary repetition or duplication"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":973,"targetId":973,"type":"tc","text":"The novelist valued {{1}}, filling the imagined town with convincing incidental details, but resisted literal transcription; she wanted plausibility rather than an exact {{2}} of a real place.","choices":[["verisimilitude","grandiloquence","anachronism"],["replica","enigma","digression"]],"answers":[["verisimilitude"],["replica"]],"explanation":"Verisimilitude is apparent realism. The contrast rejects an exact copy, or replica, without rejecting convincing invention.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"replica","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":974,"targetId":974,"type":"tc","text":"The discovery opened a {{1}} treasure trove of correspondence, not the few routine notes historians had expected; for the archivist, it was the {{2}} of a lifetime’s search.","choices":[["veritable","spurious","illusory"],["apotheosis","negation","impediment"]],"answers":[["veritable"],["apotheosis"]],"explanation":"Veritable intensifies the genuinely abundant treasure. A lifetime’s search reaching its highest fulfillment is its apotheosis, not its defeat or obstacle.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"apotheosis","meaning":"The highest realization or culmination of something"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":975,"targetId":975,"type":"tc","text":"The material is {{1}}, serving as insulation, packaging, and structural support; its usefulness therefore extends beyond any single {{2}} application.","choices":[["versatile","inflexible","obsolete"],["specialized","diverse","multifarious"]],"answers":[["versatile"],["specialized"]],"explanation":"Many uses show versatility. The contrast is with a single narrow application; diverse and multifarious already imply variety.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"specialized","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":976,"targetId":976,"type":"tc","text":"The ensemble played with such {{1}} that even a familiar score sounded newly animated; the critic praised its energy rather than technical {{2}}, since several notes were missed.","choices":[["verve","torpor","diffidence"],["perfection","incompetence","variance"]],"answers":[["verve"],["perfection"]],"explanation":"Animation requires verve. Missed notes rule out flawless technique, so perfection is the quality explicitly not praised.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"perfection","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":977,"targetId":977,"type":"tc","text":"The repeated delays caused {{1}}, but the researcher maintained a courteous {{2}}, concealing her irritation behind a calm smile.","choices":[["vexation","delectation","equanimity"],["facade","tirade","recrimination"]],"answers":[["vexation"],["facade"]],"explanation":"Delays produce annoyance. A composed outward front concealing it is a facade, not an angry speech or accusation.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"facade","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":978,"targetId":978,"type":"tc","text":"The scheme was commercially {{1}} only if its costs fell below revenue; optimistic publicity could not substitute for a {{2}} business model.","choices":[["viable","defunct","quixotic"],["sustainable","profligate","precarious"]],"answers":[["viable"],["sustainable"]],"explanation":"Financial survival requires viability and a model that can continue supporting itself. Reckless expenditure or instability would not satisfy the condition.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"sustainable","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":979,"targetId":979,"type":"tc","text":"The curator remained {{1}} even after the thefts stopped, reasoning that prolonged {{2}} could allow a new intruder to pass unnoticed.","choices":[["vigilant","complacent","somnolent"],["inattention","scrutiny","circumspection"]],"answers":[["vigilant"],["inattention"]],"explanation":"Continuing watchfulness is vigilance. Failure to attend would let intruders escape notice; scrutiny and caution would help detection.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"inattention","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":980,"targetId":980,"type":"tc","text":"The editorial’s {{1}} hostility made compromise unlikely; far from the {{2}} statement mediators had requested, it branded every opponent an enemy.","choices":[["virulent","tepid","equivocal"],["conciliatory","pugnacious","vituperative"]],"answers":[["virulent"],["conciliatory"]],"explanation":"Intense hostility is virulent. Mediators seek reconciliation, so conciliatory supplies the contrast; the other tones repeat the hostility.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":981,"targetId":981,"type":"tc","text":"The engineer was {{1}}, imagining a transport network decades before its components existed, but she did not confuse foresight with present {{2}}.","choices":[["visionary","myopic","imitative"],["feasibility","novelty","uncertainty"]],"answers":[["visionary"],["feasibility"]],"explanation":"Imagining a future system makes her visionary. The distinction is between future possibility and current practicability, not between foresight and newness.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"feasibility","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":982,"targetId":982,"type":"tc","text":"The district’s renewed {{1}} was evident in crowded shops and evening performances; descriptions of it as a place of permanent {{2}} were now obsolete.","choices":[["vitality","torpor","reticence"],["stagnation","exuberance","conviviality"]],"answers":[["vitality"],["stagnation"]],"explanation":"Active public life indicates vitality. It contradicts stalled inactivity, or stagnation, rather than exuberance or sociability.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"stagnation","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":983,"targetId":983,"type":"tc","text":"An undisclosed conflict of interest can {{1}} the credibility of a study even when its calculations are correct; mathematical precision alone cannot guarantee {{2}}.","choices":[["vitiate","bolster","authenticate"],["impartiality","complexity","replicability"]],"answers":[["vitiate"],["impartiality"]],"explanation":"A conflict can impair credibility. Correct calculations do not establish freedom from bias, or impartiality; complexity and replication are different properties.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"impartiality","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":984,"targetId":984,"type":"tc","text":"The once {{1}} host had become unusually subdued, and friends noticed the loss of her customary {{2}} before she mentioned feeling ill.","choices":[["vivacious","stolid","retiring"],["exuberance","reticence","asperity"]],"answers":[["vivacious"],["exuberance"]],"explanation":"Vivacious denotes lively spirit. A subdued manner represents loss of exuberance, not loss of habitual silence or harshness.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"exuberance","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":985,"targetId":985,"type":"tc","text":"The protest was {{1}}, its demands loudly repeated through the night; describing it as a {{2}} objection would badly misrepresent its volume and persistence.","choices":[["vociferous","tacit","diffident"],["muted","strident","clamorous"]],"answers":[["vociferous"],["muted"]],"explanation":"Loud expression is vociferous. Muted supplies the contradictory description; strident and clamorous would accurately reflect the noise.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"muted","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":986,"targetId":986,"type":"tc","text":"The coalition was {{1}}, shifting alliances weekly; apparent {{2}} after the summit proved brief, and another dispute soon exposed the agreement’s {{3}}.","choices":[["volatile","immutable","staunch"],["stability","discord","rancor"],["fragility","durability","finality"]],"answers":[["volatile"],["stability"],["fragility"]],"explanation":"Rapid change shows volatility. Brief calm gives an appearance of stability; renewed dispute reveals fragility rather than durable settlement.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"stability","meaning":"PENDING"},{"word":"fragility","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"v"},{"id":987,"targetId":987,"type":"tc","text":"Public interest began to {{1}} when the promised revelations failed to appear; even formerly {{2}} followers grew indifferent, leaving the campaign in {{3}}.","choices":[["wane","wax","burgeon"],["ardent","apathetic","lukewarm"],["obscurity","ascendancy","prominence"]],"answers":[["wane"],["ardent"],["obscurity"]],"explanation":"Interest declines, or wanes. The contrast requires previously enthusiastic followers; their departure leaves obscurity rather than greater visibility.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"obscurity","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":988,"targetId":988,"type":"tc","text":"The treasurer was {{1}} of the apparently generous offer, suspecting an {{2}} obligation; careful reading confirmed that the gift required an expensive service contract, making her caution {{3}}.","choices":[["wary","sanguine","credulous"],["implicit","imaginary","extinguished"],["warranted","gratuitous","misplaced"]],"answers":[["wary"],["implicit"],["warranted"]],"explanation":"Suspicion makes her wary. A concealed condition is implicit. Discovering the costly condition justifies the caution rather than making it needless.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"warranted","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":989,"targetId":989,"type":"tc","text":"The chair began to {{1}} after new evidence emerged; what colleagues first called {{2}} was actually a willingness to revise a position whose certainty had become {{3}}.","choices":[["waver","pontificate","persevere"],["irresolution","fortitude","obstinacy"],["indefensible","unassailable","laudable"]],"answers":[["waver"],["irresolution"],["indefensible"]],"explanation":"New doubt causes wavering. Colleagues initially mistake reasonable revision for indecision. The evidence makes the former certainty impossible to defend.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"irresolution","meaning":"PENDING"},{"word":"indefensible","meaning":"Impossible to justify reasonably"}],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":990,"targetId":990,"type":"tc","text":"The director’s {{1}} improvisations repeatedly disrupted rehearsals; actors could not predict her next change, and their attempts to impose {{2}} met with {{3}} resistance.","choices":[["wayward","methodical","tractable"],["order","caprice","novelty"],["intransigent","compliant","acquiescent"]],"answers":[["wayward"],["order"],["intransigent"]],"explanation":"Unpredictable behavior is wayward. Actors seek order, but firm refusal makes resistance intransigent rather than compliant.","difficulty":"hard","extras":[{"word":"order","meaning":"PENDING"}],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":991,"targetId":991,"type":"se","text":"After three consecutive overnight shifts, the normally energetic technician was visibly {{1}}, struggling to remain alert even during routine checks.","choices":[["weary","fatigued","indolent","nonchalant","restive","sanguine"]],"answers":[["weary","fatigued"]],"explanation":"Weary and fatigued describe exhaustion from work. Indolent would imply habitual laziness, which the long shifts and usual energy contradict.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"fatigued","meaning":"Tired through exertion"}],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":992,"targetId":992,"type":"se","text":"Unable to compel the collector to lend the painting, the curator tried to {{1}} him into agreeing, praising his generosity and gently repeating her request.","choices":[["wheedle","coax","coerce","rebuff","admonish","indemnify"]],"answers":[["wheedle","coax"]],"explanation":"Wheedle and coax express persuasion through gentle appeals or flattery. The curator cannot force compliance and is not rejecting, scolding, or compensating him.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"coax","meaning":"Persuade through gentle, persistent appeals"}],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":993,"targetId":993,"type":"se","text":"The illustrator’s {{1}} drawings show teapots dancing with umbrellas, indulging playful invention rather than attempting realistic representation.","choices":[["whimsical","fanciful","documentary","austere","pedestrian","didactic"]],"answers":[["whimsical","fanciful"]],"explanation":"Whimsical and fanciful capture playful imagination. The impossible dancing objects are neither documentary nor plainly realistic.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":994,"targetId":994,"type":"se","text":"The negotiator was {{1}}, concealing her true objective behind a series of cleverly designed concessions that cost her almost nothing.","choices":[["wily","crafty","guileless","credulous","impetuous","transparent"]],"answers":[["wily","crafty"]],"explanation":"Wily and crafty convey strategic cunning. Hidden objectives and calculated concessions rule out innocence, gullibility, rashness, or openness.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"crafty","meaning":"Clever at devising deceptive plans"}],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":995,"targetId":995,"type":"se","text":"The team’s {{1}} performance, riddled with basic errors and ending in its heaviest defeat, disappointed even supporters who had expected little.","choices":[["woeful","lamentable","mediocre","exemplary","creditable","fortuitous"]],"answers":[["woeful","lamentable"]],"explanation":"Woeful and lamentable both mark a disastrously poor performance. Mediocre means merely middling and understates the extreme failure.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"lamentable","meaning":"So poor as to deserve regret"}],"section":20,"initial":"w"},{"id":996,"targetId":996,"type":"se","text":"The pamphlet’s {{1}} stance was explicit: it portrayed foreigners of every nationality as threats and demanded their exclusion solely because they came from abroad.","choices":[["xenophobic","anti-foreign","cosmopolitan","ecumenical","impartial","philanthropic"]],"answers":[["xenophobic","anti-foreign"]],"explanation":"Xenophobic and anti-foreign both describe hostility toward foreigners as such. The blanket exclusion contradicts openness, impartiality, and inclusive concern.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"anti-foreign","meaning":"Hostile toward foreign people or influences"}],"section":20,"initial":"x"},{"id":997,"targetId":997,"type":"se","text":"The revised process should {{1}} twice as much usable material from the same quantity of ore, provided that no additional impurities enter the furnace.","choices":[["yield","produce","consume","squander","withhold","deplete"]],"answers":[["yield","produce"]],"explanation":"Yield and produce both express output. The comparison concerns material obtained, not material used up or withheld.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[{"word":"produce","meaning":"Bring forth or generate"}],"section":20,"initial":"y"},{"id":998,"targetId":998,"type":"se","text":"She approached the preservation campaign with remarkable {{1}}, devoting every free evening to it and speaking passionately about its importance.","choices":[["zeal","fervor","reticence","equanimity","lassitude","detachment"]],"answers":[["zeal","fervor"]],"explanation":"Zeal and fervor denote intense enthusiasm. Committed activity and passionate speech exclude weariness, reserve, or detachment.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"z"},{"id":999,"targetId":999,"type":"se","text":"The association’s most {{1}} members continued canvassing through heavy rain, sustained by an intense commitment that casual supporters lacked.","choices":[["zealous","ardent","diffident","apathetic","fastidious","capricious"]],"answers":[["zealous","ardent"]],"explanation":"Zealous and ardent describe strong enthusiasm. Sustained commitment contrasts with apathy and fickleness; fastidiousness concerns exacting standards.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"z"},{"id":1000,"targetId":1000,"type":"se","text":"The prize marked the {{1}} of her career, a peak in international recognition that no later achievement surpassed.","choices":[["zenith","apogee","genesis","nadir","interlude","antecedent"]],"answers":[["zenith","apogee"]],"explanation":"Zenith and apogee both mean highest point. The explicit unsurpassed peak excludes a beginning, low point, interval, or predecessor.","difficulty":"medium","extras":[],"section":20,"initial":"z"}]);
